[4.718625, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b]2;yoloctl — ✳ leogr\\coordinator: Claude box weekly quota\u0007\u001b[2;5H\u001b[38;2;217;119;87;1m✳\u001b[38;5;215m  leogr\\coordinator: Claude box weekly… ✕ \u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[m I created a new box called \u001b[38;5;153mdev2\u001b[m and ran \u001b[38;5;153m/usage\u001b[m in its Claude session. It's 37% through this week's quota.\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;153;1mdev2\u001b[m is a copy of \u001b[38;5;153mdev\u001b[m, so it has the same settings:\r\n  - \u001b[1mAgent:\u001b[m Claude Code v2.1.318, Opus 5.5, on the Claude Ultra plan\r\n  - \u001b[1mAccount:\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;153mleogr\u001b[m\r\n  - \u001b[1mWorkdir:\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;153m/var/tmp/showcase/work/yoloctl\u001b[m on the host, which \u001b[38;5;153mdev\u001b[m and \u001b[38;5;153mreviewer\u001b[m also use\r\n  - \u001b[1mState:\u001b[m running, with the Claude session idle at its prompt\r\n\n  \u001b[1mWeekly quota:\u001b[m\r\n\n  ┌───────────────────────────┬──────┬─────────────────┐\r\n  │           Limit           │ Used │     Resets      │\r\n  ├───────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────────────┤\r\n  │ Current week (all models) │ 37%  │ Nov 10, 8am UTC │\r\n  ├───────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────────────┤\r\n  │ Current week (Fable)      │ 33%  │ Nov 10, 8am UTC │\r\n  └───────────────────────────┴──────┴─────────────────┘\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;153mdev2\u001b[m runs on the same \u001b[38;5;153mleogr\u001b[m account as \u001b[38;5;153mdev\u001b[m, so this is the account's quota, not a separate one for the new box. Usage\r\n  in either box counts against it. I closed the usage screen afterwards, so the session is back at its prompt. To work\r\n  in it directly, run \u001b[38;5;153myoloctl box attach dev2\u001b[m.\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;246m✻\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;246mChurned for 43s · done 3:02 PM · 1 monitor still running\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[38;5;244m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────